shi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:608:        for a, b in cross_pairs:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:611:            events.append((1, min(ca[0], cb[0]), min(ca[1], cb[1]), a, b, \"cross\"))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:612:        for a, b in seg_cross:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:615:            events.append((1, min(pr, pr + dr), min(pc, pc + dc), a, b, \"segcross\"))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:622:            elif kind == \"segcross\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:623:                resolve_segment_cross_collision(a, b, prop)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/49/code.py:625:                resolve_cross_collision(a, b, prop)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/27/code.py:78:#    - Across examples, a solver can see three stable cues: multiple particles are processed,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/11/code.py:39:#   repeated across every sample, so humans can see it. The contact offsets are drawn from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/8/code.py:72:# - Across examples, the 5-cell plus is obviously a different symbol than the old corner L and it is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/55783887.py:52:    the segment paints the full perpendicular diagonal across the grid in its own\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/14/code.py:24:#     - 原 solver 的几何 crossing、45 度合流、90 度留空洞等逻辑都必须删除，否则会把“前景即墙”错误解释成可继续传播的碰撞。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/10/code.py:40:#     main explanatory pattern across examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:291:        \"cross_collisions\": 0,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:292:        \"segment_cross_collisions\": 0,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:435:    def resolve_cross_collision(a: int, b: int, prop) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:446:        stats[\"cross_collisions\"] += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:448:    def resolve_segment_cross_collision(a: int, b: int, prop) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:461:            raise AssertionError(\"expected crossing segment to be owned by the partner beam\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:466:        stats[\"segment_cross_collisions\"] += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:490:        cross_pairs: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:507:            cross_pairs.add(tuple(sorted((bid, obid))))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:509:        seg_cross: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:520:            seg_cross.add((bid, obid))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:542:        for a, b in cross_pairs:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:545:            events.append((1, min(ca[0], cb[0]), min(ca[1], cb[1]), a, b, \"cross\"))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:546:        for a, b in seg_cross:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:549:            events.append((1, min(pr, pr + dr), min(pc, pc + dc), a, b, \"segcross\"))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:556:            elif kind == \"segcross\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:557:                resolve_segment_cross_collision(a, b, prop)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:559:                resolve_cross_collision(a, b, prop)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/29/code.py:590:    - Whenever beams collide on a cell or cross diagonally, the interaction point is handled as in the symbol variant:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/24/code.py:41:#   of having to estimate ratios across very different sizes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/24/code.py:68:# - Across 2-4 examples a human can see:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/24/code.py:93:#   score across consecutive pairs; this should stay positive if the D7 chain really\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/7/code.py:74:# - Across examples, the red border pixel consistently predicts whether the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/24/code.py:252:    - The path geometry is stable within a segment, but not across segments: the first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/17/code.py:43:#    Across 2-4 examples, a human can see vertical segmentation, regular black separator columns,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/12/code.py:51:#      the next frame's entry gap is reached exactly, without crossing any frame cell or previously used trail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ca8f78db.py:45:    Treat black pixels as unknown, infer the unique smallest rectangular period that agrees with every non-black pixel, and tile it across the full grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/ca8f78db.py:80:    \"\"\"Sample the periodic tile and render it across the full grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/15/code.py:47:   - Original row parser assumed each stripe row is uniform across width. Still true.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/15/code.py:63:   transforms are global, count-controlled, and easy to compare across examples:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/15/code.py:75:     stripe's color becomes split across disjoint radial positions, which cannot happen in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/15/code.py:108:            raise ValueError(\"each stripe row must be uniform across width\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/15/code.py:113:                raise ValueError(\"each stripe row must be uniform across width\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/15/code.py:204:        # rotation can split that color across separated radial positions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:17:#   the corridor. Original logic would cross both the launch gap and the later\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:24:#   (1) a real particle that visibly crosses the 3-cell launch buffer and a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:48:#   one row that crosses a 3-wide hole against another row that stops at a 4/5-\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:162:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles through shifted corridors with bounded gap crossing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/33/code.py:170:      across unsupported runs of width at most 3.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:385:            assert not (is_diag_a and is_diag_b), \"diagonal 90-degree pairs should cross geometrically\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:463:    def resolve_cross_collision(a: int, b: int, prop) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:469:        assert u != (0, 0), \"crossing diagonals should produce a forward direction\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:477:    def resolve_segment_cross_collision(a: int, b: int, prop) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:496:        assert u != (0, 0), \"segment cross should produce a forward direction\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:530:        cross_pairs: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:548:            cross_pairs.add((a, b))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:550:        seg_cross: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:561:            seg_cross.add((bid, obid))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:584:        for a, b in cross_pairs:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:587:            events.append((1, min(ca[0], cb[0]), min(ca[1], cb[1]), a, b, \"cross\"))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:589:        for a, b in seg_cross:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:592:            events.append((1, min(pr, pr + dr), min(pc, pc + dc), a, b, \"segcross\"))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:599:            elif kind == \"segcross\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:600:                resolve_segment_cross_collision(a, b, prop)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/18/code.py:602:                resolve_cross_collision(a, b, prop)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:26:#    - D9 changes a pass-through crossing into a mandatory branch point. Concretely,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:27:#      if a particle is about to enter a BG crossing cell and that crossing exposes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:29:#      immediately instead of moving straight across the crossing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:31:#      the Z is encoded as two open crossings:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:36:#      crossing and continue right forever. The combo solver instead turns up at that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:37:#      crossing, then turns right again at the upper crossing, producing a zig-zag\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:53:#      second corner of a Z path is also an open crossing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:56:#      letting shafts cross fake rows or their intended target row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:65:#      fake, so the vertical shaft never crosses another active real row and therefore\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:72:#      one-sided crossing and the particle relocates onto a parallel row to the right of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:73:#      the shaft. Across a few examples, the zig-zag offset is visible without relying\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:79:#      separated in both row intervals and columns, intersections stay readable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:124:    \"\"\"Return a forced turn through the next open crossing, if any.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:296:    - If the next BG cell is an open crossing with exactly one perpendicular corridor,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:302:    - Z corridors are encoded as two one-sided open crossings, so the particle zig-zags\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/21/code.py:441:    \"\"\"Build an open-crossing Z: right -> up/down -> right.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/11/code.py:43:#    - Content colors are unique across cups to keep matching legible in multi-cup scenes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/11/code.py:68:#    - Across examples, the long ray length tracks cup size rather than number of controls, which is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/11/code.py:83:#      Generator keeps control color different from its own border color and unique across cups.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/e4075551.py:27:    Draw the colored rectangle defined by four control pixels and connect its interior to the red pivot with a grey cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/e4075551.py:36:    - Paint the top and bottom sides across the full left-to-right span,