)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/25/code.py:506:    - When a beam would hit another beam, or two diagonal steps would geometrically cross, the contested meeting point is not painted.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/16/code.py:223:    # Keep the visual grouping obvious across examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/446ef5d2/7/code.py:54:  fully rect_col left edge, etc. Repeated evidence across many tiles makes the structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/0d87d2a6.py:14:    - Draw each guide row or column across the whole grid in the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/10/code.py:46:#       the added ambiguity is small and repeated across samples\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/78332cb0/10/code.py:48:#     - old _find_sep assumed a non-bg color forms full rows/cols across the board;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/29/code.py:234:    - Repeat every decoded phase across the full output canvas of size (3H-2)x(3W-2), using that glyph's own input color as the lattice foreground.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/5b526a93.py:35:    Complete a rectangular table of identical sprites by stamping teal copies at the empty row-column intersections.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/45a5af55/9/code.py:97:Across 2-4 examples, a human can see:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/26/code.py:44:#   - Generator prefers corner gaps and rejects beam intersections, so the fused\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/26/code.py:61:#     share cells or geometrically cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/26/code.py:66:#     number of frame openings, and that same count repeats across all beams from a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/26/code.py:395:            assert not (is_diag_a and is_diag_b), \"two diagonal beams must cross geometrically, not collide on one cell\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e1