an can see that the input is made of tall vertical bars, not horizontal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/eval/642d658d.py:151:    \"\"\"Grow one isolated noise component without crossing blocked or prior noise.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:32:#              -> keep only a large cross window (plus/H) or a large diamond window (X/4corners)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:38:#          combo output  = cross-shaped lattice silhouette with a 6x6 black hole in the middle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:49:#    - The erase stage uses only two large window families: cross or diamond.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:52:#      two glyphs, so the branch split is balanced and repeated across samples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:77:#        2. the surviving lattice silhouette flips between a cross and a diamond depending\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:138:    \"\"\"Use orthogonal middle-row arms for cross windows; diagonal/corner-only forms get diamonds.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:140:    return \"cross\" if bool(motif[1, 0]) else \"diamond\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:150:    if kind == \"cross\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:173:    - Repeat that phase tile across a 16x16 black canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:174:    - Use the glyph's visible symmetry family to choose an erase window: plus/H keep a cross, X/four-corners keep a diamond.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/18/code.py:222:    \"cross\": (\"plus\", \"H\"),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/28/code.py:37:#   the current direction. At most 2 unsupported cells may be crossed; the 3rd\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/28/code.py:51:#   repeated across many lanes in every sample.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/28/code.py:263:    \"\"\"Move magenta particles through dashed narrow corridors with bounded gap crossing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/45/code.py:31:#   down. When one horizontal and one vertical ray meet, the crossing cell is cleared\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/45/code.py:39:#   appear in each instance, plus at least one horizontal/vertical crossing. That keeps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/45/code.py:49:#   turn beams; they only punch a 1-cell hole at perpendicular crossings. This lets the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/45/code.py:50:#   solver collapse to fixed-direction propagation with blocked crossing cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/45/code.py:58:#   and at least one crossing. A human comparing input/output can therefore see that top\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/45/code.py:64:#   Frames keep >=2 cells of clearance, crossings happen only on background cells, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/45/code.py:73:#   - every perpendicular crossing lands on background and never on a seed cell;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/45/code.py:238:    cross_same_tick = 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/45/code.py:239:    cross_with_painted = 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/45/code.py:295:                cross_same_tick += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/45/code.py:326:                cross_with_painted += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/45/code.py:340:        \"blocked_crossings\": len(blocked),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/45/code.py:341:        \"same_tick_crossings\": cross_same_tick,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/45/code.py:342:        \"retro_crossings\": cross_with_painted,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_c