epeats across examples instead of exploding\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/ba97ae07.py:16:    Swap the visible color of the crossing area between two perpendicular full-span bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/ba97ae07.py:22:    - Their rectangular crossing is uniformly one of the two foreground colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/ba97ae07.py:25:    - Preserve the grid except for the crossing rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/ba97ae07.py:26:    - Recolor every crossing pixel to the other foreground color, making the hidden bar visible there.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/ba97ae07.py:29:    - The crossing is exactly the intersection of all-foreground rows and all-foreground columns; its current color identifies the bar on top, so the output flips it to the other bar color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/ba97ae07.py:44:    crossing = g[np.ix_(full_rows, full_cols)]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/ba97ae07.py:45:    crossing_colors = np.unique(crossing)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/ba97ae07.py:46:    assert crossing_colors.size == 1, \"crossing must have a single visible color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/ba97ae07.py:47:    visible_color = int(crossing_colors[0])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/ba97ae07.py:48:    assert visible_color in fg_colors, \"crossing color must be foreground\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/ba97ae07.py:72:    crossing = t_h * t_v\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/ba97ae07.py:73:    bg_count = H * W - (t_h * W + t_v * H - crossing)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/ba97ae07.py:74:    h_count = t_h * W - (0 if top_is_h else crossing)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/ba97ae07.py:75:    v_count = t_v * H - (crossing if top_is_h else 0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/eee78d87/23/code.py:72:#      consistently altered across examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/21/code.py:26:#    - If 