color leads to different templates, so a human can reject\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/2/code.py:36:#     - The trail color is fixed grey across all samples so the extra color has a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/2/code.py:39:#       contain visible grey trail, while the output must contain visible actor path\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/2/code.py:69:#     - Using grey for historical footprint and actor for the answer path keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/2/code.py:382:    - The grey trail in the input is only historical evidence. The required output is a clean single frame containing the final sprite plus every cell visited by the head during the remaining simulation, drawn in the actor color as a continuous orthogonal path.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/0a938d79.py:21:    - Their placement determines whether the bars run across rows or columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/4/code.py:25:#     intersection would erase every colored layer and collapse the task. The fused solver\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/4/code.py:307:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/26/code.py:748:def _cross_limit(rad, h, w):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/26/code.py:752:def _anchor_from_dist(rad, h, w, depth, gap, edge_dist, cross_start):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/26/code.py:754:        return edge_dist, cross_start\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/26/code.py:756:        return (h - 1) - edge_dist, cross_start\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/26/code.py:758:        return cross_start, edge_dist\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/26/code.py:759:    return cross_start, (w - 1) - edge_dist\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b9e38dc0/26/code.py:768:    cross_cap = _cross_limit(rad, h, w)\n/home/lixinyu/s