cit: grey walls create a bent 5-step path, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/1/code.py:67:#      wall evidence local and prevents the grid from becoming cluttered with many crossing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/d07ae81c.py:80:    - Original marker pixels remain unchanged, including where diagonal paths cross them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/39/code.py:27:#      5-row band across the full width, so the output is 5x30 instead of 30x30.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/39/code.py:37:#    - Column-based lane extraction no longer applies; every lane operation must switch to fixed row bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/39/code.py:240:      lattice slots first, proceeding from left to right across the lane.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/2/code.py:35:#        (2,0). The key difference is \"match border colors across bands, ignore marker color\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/2/code.py:49:#    - Marker slots remain unique across templates, so each output block gets at most one stamp.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/2/code.py:52:#    - Across examples, the same marker color appears under multiple different outputs, which makes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/caa06a1f.py:16:    Continue the translational pattern across the canvas and shift its phase one column right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/5/code.py:36:#    also \"different regions now repeat the same cross-region color order\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/5/code.py:52:#      the fill palette is pooled across regions\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/5/code.py:69:#    - the shared palette is inferable because the same band order reappears across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/39/code.py:95:  to notice across a few examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/39/code.py: