ted cases so multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/10/code.py:8:#   pixels are scattered across all three tile columns rather than one color per column. The solver must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/10/code.py:19:#   3. `template identity can be inferred per column` no longer holds. The solver must pool counts across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/65b59efc/10/code.py:64:    - Marker color no longer names the template directly. Instead, group all markers by color across the whole\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/19/code.py:250:      same-color pixel whose reflected partner across that slot axis is absent.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/7/code.py:46:#    - The original solver was indifferent to intermediate path crossings. The combo is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/7/code.py:47:#      not: if trails crossed sprite cells in the input, the visible ray would become\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/4/code.py:25:#   same center and orthogonal cross. The rule remains a single local test with no hidden state,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/4/code.py:40:#   Across 2-4 training pairs, a human can compare solid 3x3 patches against almost-identical\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/4/code.py:52:#   An input-first generator is safer than the original output-first cross generator. Solid 3x3\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/1818057f/4/code.py:103:    - The decisive test is full 3x3 completeness, not the thinner '+' cross hidden inside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/10/code.py:24:  colors from one fixed visible spectrum order and repeats that order across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/1e0a9b12.py:25:      columns or crossing each other.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/21/code.py:61:#      the walls persist across frames while markers disappear as consumed.\n/home/lixin