rs must avoid all\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/17/code.py:46:#    - For collision events, the generator reserves the entire blue-cross footprint plus the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/17/code.py:48:#      between sprites, blue crosses, and maroon singleton marks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/17/code.py:51:#      triangle causes two shifted impacts, and repeated impacts on empty bg create a cross\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/17/code.py:52:#      instead of a point. Samples contain multiple blue crosses, multiple maroon singleton\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/17/code.py:55:#    - Output markers are forced to be disjoint: blue cross footprints do not overlap sprites,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/17/code.py:56:#      other crosses, or singleton maroon cells. This keeps the scene legible despite the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/17/code.py:64:#    - `main()` allows collision crosses to clip at borders for robustness, but the generator\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/17/code.py:65:#      always chooses full in-bounds crosses so training samples show the intended shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/17/code.py:146:def _collision_cross(center: tuple[int, int]) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], ...]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/17/code.py:151:def _paint_collision_cross(out: np.ndarray, center: tuple[int, int], color: int) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/17/code.py:153:    for r, c in _collision_cross(center):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/17/code.py:203:            _paint_collision_cross(out, dest, COLLISION_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/17/code.py:224:    - If multiple projectiles land on the same empty background cell, that collision becomes a blue (1) cross centered there; a lone empty-bg landing becomes a 