ches to an exact hollow-rectangle test:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/30/code.py:55:#    Across 2-4 examples, a human sees three repeated cues:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/25/code.py:37:#   their centroid sets do not create cross-group aligned-clear links, preventing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/25/code.py:71:# - Across 2-4 training examples, a human can infer that lines go through blob\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/25/code.py:83:# - At least one color is reused across multiple shape groups, so the combo inputs\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/25/code.py:760:def _cross_group_alignment_exists(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/25/code.py:788:            if _cross_group_alignment_exists(global_centers, info[\"centers\"]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2ba387bc/14/code.py:97:   - Reusing colors across separate objects is safe because padding prevents accidental\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/2bcee788.py:15:    Mirror the main object across the side indicated by red marker pixels and turn the background green.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/2bcee788.py:25:    - Reflect every main-object pixel across that axis, then recolor all remaining black background green.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/11/code.py:44:#    Across a few examples, a human sees three parallel source bands in the input and three\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/14/code.py:39:      - the source palette is small enough for repeated evidence across 2-4 samples, but not so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/cbded52d.py:23:    \"\"\"Complete straight same-color marker segments across the tiled lattice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/28/code.py:202:    Distribute matches across the 4 frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/52/code.py:59:#    - Across examples, the outside sprites are visibly