/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/9/code.py:42:#      the simulation must be global across all shapes. Per-color order is used only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:17:#    geometry becomes a two-stage nested cross:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:18:#    - stage 1 marker: a thick outer cross shell in color 8,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:19:#    - stage 2 marker: a thinner inner cross in color 0, sharing the same center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:29:#    Only one nested marker pair is injected, both crosses are axis-aligned and concentric, and the arm\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:31:#    rule obvious across 2-4 examples without exploding the hypothesis space. The shape change remains visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:32:#    because the shell is a real cross silhouette, not a barely perturbed rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:35:#    - \"every marker cell lies inside one bbox that is fully hidden\" is false: corners of the cross bbox stay visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:36:#    - \"output equals the full hidden rectangle\" changes to \"output equals the inner cross bbox, with only cross\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:41:#    The generator builds the clean symmetric canvas first, then chooses nested cross masks that are fully in-bounds,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:44:#    - stage 1 treats the whole outer cross footprint (shell + inner cross) as hidden,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:45:#    - stage 2 treats only the inner cross as hidden,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:50:#    the inner plus bbox, so across examples the same \"peel outer cross, then peel inner cross\" story is directly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:54:#    two-color cross pair, which is sparse enough to avoid clutter and rigid enough to be instantly separable from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:58:#    least one inner cell whose raw reflection witnesses are all trapped inside the outer cross. That makes the staged\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:61:#    - color 8 appears exactly on the outer-shell cells of one thick cross,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:62:#    - color 0 appears exactly on the cells of one thinner concentric inner cross,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:63:#    - the union of colors {8,0} is itself a valid thick cross footprint,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:72:def _cross_mask(h: int, w: int, thickness: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:91:def _cross_params(mask: np.ndarray) -> tuple[tuple[int, int, int, int], int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:108:    expected = _cross_mask(h, w, thickness)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:113:def _full_cross_from_bbox(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:117:    return _paint_mask(shape, int(r0), int(c0), _cross_mask(int(r1 - r0 + 1), int(c1 - c0 + 1), thickness))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:120:def _nested_cross_markers(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:124:    inner_bbox, inner_t = _cross_params(inner_mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:127:    outer_bbox, outer_t = _cross_params(outer_union)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:137:    outer_full = _full_cross_from_bbox(g.shape, outer_bbox, outer_t)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:138:    inner_full = _full_cross_from_bbox(g.shape, inner_bbox, inner_t)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:215:    Peel a nested pair of cross-shaped markers and return the innermost hidden patch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:219:    - The occluder is now a concentric two-layer cross: a thick outer shell in color 8 surrounds a thinner inner cross in color 0.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:220:    - Cross corners inside each bbox can remain visible background pattern; only the cross footprints are actually hidden.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:223:    - Detect the nested outer-shell/inner-core cross pair and infer the reflected strip start while ignoring both marker colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:225:    - Then restore the inner cross on the partially repaired grid and output the inner cross bbox with those repaired cells inserted.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:228:    The two marker colors are two occlusion layers over the same symmetric texture. Some inner-cross cells cannot trust the raw\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:233:    outer_bbox, outer_t, inner_bbox, inner_t = _nested_cross_markers(g)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:236:    outer_full = _full_cross_from_bbox(g.shape, outer_bbox, outer_t)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:237:    inner_full = _full_cross_from_bbox(g.shape, inner_bbox, inner_t)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:262:# --- CFG: cross sizes ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:327:        outer_local = _cross_mask(outer_h, outer_w, _OUTER_THICKNESS)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:328:        inner_local = _cross_mask(inner_h, inner_w, _INNER_THICKNESS)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/0934a4d8/10/code.py:431:    outer_ful