/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/18/code.py:65:   - Across examples, a human sees that the output changes only in the right half while the left\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC1_code/train/623ea044.py:28:    - The lone pixel provides both the intersection point and the color for the two full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/13/code.py:214:        cross = int(dr1 * dc2 - dc1 * dr2)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/13/code.py:215:        assert cross != 0, \"path must stay axis-aligned\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/13/code.py:216:        signs.append(cross)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/28/code.py:55:#   output simultaneously shows (a) near/far band colors crossing over by rank\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/291dc1e1/28/code.py:59:#   \"body color moved across bands\" signal from incidental decorative pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/32/code.py:46:#      block masks must therefore be unique across different slots; the generator enforces that, while\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/32/code.py:408:    - Distractors are isolated one-pixel foreground cells. Piece colors may repeat across sprites, but\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/14/code.py:49:#     - output shows one chained trail of the same two-blob layout across multiple bars\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/14/code.py:78:#   - bars visited by different sprites reserve non-overlapping x-intervals across all iterative steps\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/14/code.py:82:#   - repeated placements of the same disconnected layout across different bars make iteration legible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7c66cb00/14/code.py:87:#   - the chain is short and repeated across samples, so humans can infer \"new outer color drives the next step\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/25/code.py:66:#   - Across examples, a human can see