ough the palette is compressed and roles reuse colors across wallpaper, borders, and sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/15/code.py:417:    \"\"\"Allocate a 5-6 color palette with explicit cross-role reuse.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/26/code.py:28:#   and \"split-across-edges instead of cropped\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/26/code.py:50:#   Across 2-4 examples, a solver can see three stable cues: marker groups are always 2-3 cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/26/code.py:292:    - After translation, any pixel that crosses a grid edge wraps to the opposite side; anchors stay fixed, source cells are cleared, and existing non-background cells are not overwritten.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/24/code.py:8:#    The seed task had two geometric families, and every sprite switched to the opposite family while\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/24/code.py:34:#    The viewer sees the same three color triples recurring on the same sprite shape. Across examples,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/25/code.py:233:        \"cross_overwrite_cells\": len(overwritten_cells),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/25/code.py:234:        \"cross_overwrite_events\": overwritten_events,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/25/code.py:590:    overwrite_cells = combo_stats[\"cross_overwrite_cells\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/20/code.py:64:  - Across 2-3 examples, the repeated pattern \"same hole shape, different wall\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/8/code.py:62:#    - Across samples, matched sprites survive but show alternating fill pixels, while one similarly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/13/code.py:67:#    - Across examples, a human sees only two colors, yet each local red/blue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/13/code.py:81:#      the cycle, the \"cross-color pairing\" rule is directly supported inside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/17/code.py:9:#   1. Detect the bars crossing the long base row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/17/code.py:80:# - Across several examples a solver can see that:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/20/code.py:44:#      repeats across 3 distinct sides. That makes the side-driven rotation cue explicit:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/1/code.py:151:    - The transformation uses two structural levels at once: outer contour decides the group, while enclosed-hole count decides the partner inside the opposite group. Colors alone are insufficient because the same palette is reused across the two hole-count members of each family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/26/code.py:236:    - Skip across any visible same-color prefix, then fill remaining background cells with that segment color until the boundary or another foreground object.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/44/code.py:82:#   - Across examples, a human can see that:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/24/code.py:27:#       placement across different edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/24/code.py:73:#       sprites or fill values, so humans can spot it across 2-4 examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/24/code.py:87:#     - Exactly one palette color repeats across entries: the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/24/code.py:277:      gather separated edge clues, infer the marker color shared across them, decode each segment's direction, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:426:    \"transform\": \"mirror s across the red marker axis (vertical/horizontal red line) or point-reflect around an isolated red pixel; paint the mirrored pixels onto bg\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:806:    \"summary\": \"Find sprites connected to grey path endpoints, match source sprites by border color to destination center color, transfer source center color to destination center, then delete unconnected sprites.\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:809:    \"dst\": \"colored bordered sprites d connected to grey path endpoints (path endpoint must connect to sprite's center position)\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:816:    \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify grey connected path and sprites at path endpoints (d); Step 2: for each d, find s where s.border_color == d.center_color; Step 3: copy s.center_color to d.center; Step 4: delete all sprites not connected to grey path\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:825:    \"src2\": \"all sprites not connected to grey path\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1052:    \"transform\": \"if projectile hits opposing sprite, recolor entire sprite to maroon; if two projectiles collide, paint blue at intersection\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1191:    \"summary\": \"Solid 3x3 colored blocks connected to teal pipelines are split into hollow cross (stays) and solid four-star (moves to pipeline's other end); incomplete shapes at pipeline ends are completed with their counterpart.\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1198:    \"transform\": \"split s into hollow cross (center + 4 cardinal neighbors) staying at original position, and solid four-star (4 diagonal corners) moving to d\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1209:    \"src2\": \"hollow cross or solid four-star already at one end of teal pipeline s\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1214:    \"transform2\": \"place the complementary shape (four-star if cross exists, cross if four-star exists) at d with same color as s\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1270:    \"summary\": \"Four endpoints of a teal cross emit same-colored spiral trajectories clockwise, filling the grid like a kaleidoscope with one-pixel spacing between trails.\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1272:    \"src\": \"four endpoint pixels of the teal cross s\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1343:    \"trajectory\": \"paint s.color along entire diagonal path; when two paths collide at 90 degrees, both turn 45 degrees with one pixel gap at intersection and form diagonal line using single pixels; when paths meet at 45 degrees, paths merge without gap and both turn 22.5 degrees forming line using 2x2 pixel blocks\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1354:    \"notes\": \"Critical collision rule: for 90-degree collisions with 45-degree turns, there is a one-pixel gap at intersection and paths are drawn as single diagonal pixels; for 45-degree collisions with 22.5-degree turns, there is no gap and paths are drawn as 2x2 pixel blocks\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc-agi-2-eval-annotations-merge.json:1481:    \"notes\": \"crossings prefer yellow-control rays; otherwise original-vs-filled crossings use the more fragmented repaired line, and marker-bracketed filled gaps beat unmarked pure fills\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/15/code.py:21:#    from the segment's intersection row with the baseline, not from x-position. The solver must:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/15/code.py:35:#    exactly one baseline intersection per object, which avoids ambiguous slot anchors, and excluding\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/15/code.py:62:#    A human looking at the examples sees a vertical pink spine and several colored slashes crossing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/15/code.py:72:#   centered diagonal segments, so every object has one unique intersection cell on the baseline.\n/ho