ars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/2/code.py:59:       numbers, so every bar has a unique center column crossing the base row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/2/code.py:72:   - Bars are odd-height rectangles centered on the base row, so every bar crosses the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/2/code.py:78:   - Across examples, the output is not monotone in height and not monotone in width.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/2/code.py:84:   - Bars are solid odd-by-odd rectangles crossing the detected base row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/2/code.py:183:    Sort bars by pixel area and redistribute them across fixed colored slots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/9/code.py:64:#    - Across examples, humans can see two stable signals: outside pieces are hollow while output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/35ab12c3/30/code.py:317:    and its interior crosses only background or same-color input cells. After all\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/25/code.py:72:#    Across examples, the input always shows a single dense guided rectangle away from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/9/code.py:76:#      colors. This provides an explicit cross-reference humans can read.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/7/code.py:227:    assert anc0 == anc1, \"generator guarantees identical anchor bboxes across the two prototypes\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/16/code.py:88:Across a few examples, a human should notice two coupled facts:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/10/code.py:39:#    Across examples, inputs show clearly multicolor pieces while outputs collapse to a single frame\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/26/code.py:42:#    A human sees two fixed-color guide segments whose common length changes across examples, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/80a900e0/1/code.py:69:     number of painted cells contributed by middle emitters across the whole instance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/9/code.py:37:#          2. keep only baseline-crossing solid centered rectangles as true bars,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/9/code.py:72:#    - Across 2-4 examples, a human can see three stable facts:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/9/code.py:73:#      1. the corner staircase persists and flips orientation across some examples,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/9/code.py:75:#      3. only the baseline-crossing bars get permuted, and their permutation follows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/9/code.py:249:    - Only baseline-crossing solid centered rectangles are sortable bars.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/37/code.py:28:# - Observability and cleanliness: the same small color family recurs across samples, so the cyclic\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/fc7cae8d/31/code.py:49:#    Across samples, the carrier edge can vary independently of the target side, so the human-visible cue is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/21/code.py:38:#    - Anchor colors are chosen from one fixed visible ordered pair across samples, making\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/21/code.py:68:#      quadrants, at least one repeated anchor color across quadrants, nonzero cross-color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/21/code.py:318:    cross_overlap = 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/21/code.py:327:            cross_overlap += overlap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/21/code.py:333:        \"cross_color_overlap\": int(cross_overlap),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/21/code.py:536:    cross_overlap = 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/21/code.py:543:            cross_overlap += overlap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/21/c