 are unique across the 2 types, so the lookup key is never\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/4/code.py:96:#    - Body colors are unique across types and disjoint from anchor colors, so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/6e453dd6.py:49:    - For each row spanned by such a hole, emit a red ray across the entire right half of the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/31/code.py:160:    Connect the blue endpoint pairs across their diagonals, tint the cells next to magenta crossings with a shared bridge color, and let the perpendicular rays fade from magenta into blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/31/code.py:163:    - The background is the most common color and is never 1, 6, or 8. Blue endpoint pixels form one or more diagonal pairs. Magenta pixels that lie on those diagonals are the active crossings; off-diagonal magenta pixels are inert distractors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:24:#    - Anchors remain 1-3 colors and sprites remain 3-5, so anchor colors repeat across multiple\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:47:#    - Across examples, the large obvious color consistently matches the anchor that governs motion.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:689:    cross_count = 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:695:            cross_count += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/581f7754/20/code.py:701:    if len(anchor_colors) >= 2 and cross_count == 0:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dbff022c/35/code.py:310:    \"\"\"Maximum number of peeled layers across all holes.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/4/code.py:21:#    Seed task objects are centered vertical rectangles that intersect the base row across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/4/code.py:32:#    The a=2 example above becomes a sideways cross whose left tip lies on the slot anchor:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/4/code.py:50:#      specifically makes each input cross touch the base row at exactly one cell: its bottom\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/4/code.py:52:#    - bbox_h was previously the bar height. For these bottom-anchored crosses, bbox_h is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/4/code.py:67:#    movable objects are now crosses with varying arm lengths. Across examples, the shorter\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/4/code.py:68:#    crosses migrate to the leftmost slots exactly as before, yet the outputs are no longer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/4/code.py:69:#    upright: each reassigned cross lies sideways because the anchor is the tip on the base\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/4/code.py:70:#    row, not the cross center. This makes the fusion readable from a few examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/4/code.py:80:def _cross_rel(arm: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/4/code.py:202:        raise ValueError(\"crosses do not fit\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/4/code.py:225:        rel = _cross_rel(int(arm))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/db695cfb.py:16:    - Where the diagonal crosses a trigger pixel, emit perpendicular diagonal rays (in the trigger's color) extending to the grid boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/2/code.py:15:#     - Suppose shape family A is an L-like 4x4 template and family B is a cross-like 4x4 template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/2/code.py:23:#       swap target pairs across shape families: A receives B's legend target (yellow, maroon), and B\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/c7f57c3e/2/code.py:58:#     - Across examples, the stable invariants are: same-shape grouping, legend decoding, and swapping of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/68bc2e87.py:145:    \"\"\"Sample one frame