e.py:73:#     not diagonals, and that magenta spreads as full row/column crosses rather\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/1/code.py:79:#     blue-backbone / magenta-cross decomposition readable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/1/code.py:98:    Connect same-color straight endpoint pairs, then emit orthogonal cross rays from differently-colored pixels on those paths.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/1/code.py:108:    - Blue identifies the axis-aligned backbone, and magenta trigger pixels convert that backbone into a cross-emitter: the cross keeps propagating through the row/column geometry even when some cells on its route are already occupied by the blue segment.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/1/code.py:227:def _cross_fill_cells(trigger: tuple[int, int], path_cells: set[tuple[int, int]], H: int, W: int) -> set[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/1/code.py:335:        cross_cells = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/1/code.py:337:            cross_cells.update(_cross_fill_cells(tp, path_set, H, W))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/1/code.py:339:        if any(rc in occupied or rc in drawn for rc in cross_cells):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/1/code.py:346:        drawn.update(cross_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/31f7f899/12/code.py:70:#    - Across a few training pairs, a human can see that outputs are not globally\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/13/code.py:35:#    - Center colors must be unique across types; otherwise destination markers would be ambiguous.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/13/code.py:62:#      This makes the lookup cue repeated and explicit across copies.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a251c730/13/code.py:69:#    - Every sprite's center color is unique across types and appears as a destination marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/c