e isolated singletons, stay in-bounds, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:45:#    unless complete-first changes at least one crossing relative to fragmented-first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:47:#    The scene is intentionally sparse: three one-cell-thick lines, two crossings, and two isolated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:52:#    the horizontal ones in the input, and it consistently takes the crossing after repair. Because the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:296:                assert adj_other, f\"dangling endpoint ({r},{c}) color {color}: not on boundary or crossing\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:299:    crossing_colors = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:308:                    crossing_colors.add(a)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:309:                    crossing_colors.add(b)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:311:        assert color in crossing_colors, f\"color {color} has no crossing with any other color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:316:    Rebuild a one-cell-thick rectilinear line network by recoloring singleton markers, repeatedly filling supported gaps, and resolving crossings in favor of the more complete color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:330:    Key insight: The singleton markers only tell you which fragments belong together; the real challenge is that one repair can enable the next, so the network must be completed to a fixed point, and crossings consistently follow the line that already looks less broken.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:355:    crossing_gain = int(np.count_nonzero(combo != fragmented))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/23/code.py:356:    return cascade_gain, crossing_gain\n/home/lixin