lumn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D7/0/code.py:36:#    - Stripe length remains 2-4 so the cycle still has repeated support across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D7/0/code.py:63:#    - Across examples, the human-visible difference is that the color cycle is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D3/2/code.py:51:#    - Across examples, every movable object visibly becomes a ring/frame with a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/1/code.py:380:    cross = int(dw if vertical else dh)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D5/2/code.py:42:#       at least 3 collision sites per sample and spreads them across at least two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D5/2/code.py:523:    # First guarantee coverage across at least two groups.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/291dc1e1/D9/0/code.py:15:# - Original input had one border row and one border column crossing at a corner,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/291dc1e1/D9/0/code.py:16:#   but the crossing cell was a third marker color. The solver used that unique\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/291dc1e1/D9/0/code.py:65:# - Across examples, the long line may be color 1 or color 2, and its orientation\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D7/0/code.py:59:    - Across 2-4 examples, a human can still infer that sprites align to matching anchor colors exactly as before.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D4/2/code.py:44:#    along diagonals and the arrowhead itself points diagonally. Across 2-4\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D17/0/code.py:56:#      few train pairs because the same three colors recur with repeated sprites across examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D22/2/code.py:232:    Move a triangular sprite across the grid, consuming aligned marker pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/2/code.py:40:# - Connector colors come from a small reusable palette. Colors can repeat across different shapes, so the key is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/2/code.py:52:#   and `(h, w, connector_color, connector_offset)` is unique across all pieces.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/2/code.py:254:    max_cross = min(MAX_SHORT_DIM, short_dim - 2)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/2/code.py:257:        for cr in range(1, max_cross + 1):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/2/code.py:326:        cross = w if long_is_rows else h\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/2/code.py:327:        cross_max = short_dim - cross - 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/2/code.py:328:        if cross_max < 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/2/code.py:330:        cross0 = random.randint(1, cross_max)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/2/code.py:334:            new_item[\"c\"] = int(cross0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/2/code.py:337:            new_item[\"r\"] = int(cross0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D7/1/code.py:69:    - If the translated sprite would cross the old frame, expand the output grid on that side instead of clipping it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/0/code.py:90:    - Horizontal red line => reflect across that row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/0/code.py:91:    - Vertical red line => reflect across that column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D17/1/code.py:52:#    bottommost cell of the border run, the relation is consistent across examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D15/0/code.py:37:#      This keeps the task inferable from a few examples instead of branching across many\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D15/0/code.py:56:#    - Across examples, both input connectors visibly sit on the same side of their bodies.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D7/2/code.py:48:#       per sample, but still varies that edge across samples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D5/0/code.py:249:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D15/2/code.py:28:#   The bar length still has only 1-3 choices and must match across sprites, which keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D15/1/code.py:292:    Continue a marker-consuming arrow simulation whose sprite template alternates across snapshots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:14:    - Horizontal red line -> reflect payload across that row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D9/2/code.py:15:    - Vertical red line -> reflect payload across that column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D17/2/code.py:61:#    The number of mapped colors is small (2-3), repeated across several sprites per grid, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D5/2/code.py:210:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D3/0/code.py:39:- To make the new behavior visible and logically necessary, at least one hole size is duplicated across different frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D3/0/code.py:70:- Repeated hole sizes across different frames prevent the samples from being explainable as one global cavity again.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D3/0/code.py:92:- Assumption: some sizes repeat across frames, otherwise the extra grouping stage would be unnecessary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D3/0/code.py:125:    # Base color = dominant non-bg color by total area across all its disconnected frame pieces.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D14/2/code.py:35:#     - Anchor offsets vary across colors whenever possible, and at least one non-central anchor\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/1/code.py:46:    Sort vertical bars by height and redistribute them across fixed colored slots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/1/code.py:57:    is split across two loci so that the slot and the incoming bar exchange colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/1/code.py:205:    # Heights start at 3 so every bar has a visible body separate from its baseline crossing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D13/1/code.py:53:#      erase body-body intersections, so those cells must be intercepted first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D13/1/code.py:62:#      intersection and no extension above/left of the base.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D13/1/code.py:68:#      the merged bodies cross; every generated example contains at least one red\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D13/1/code.py:72:#    - Only one extra layer of meaning is added: red marks crossings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D12/3/code.py:30:#    The allowed spans are restricted to 3..5 and each puzzle reuses 2-3 span values across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/800d221b/_variant_lib.py:195:def _layout_cross_hub() -> Layout:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/800d221b/_variant_lib.py:379:        return _layout_cross_hub()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D7/0/code.py:60:# - Across examples, the merged shape is the same as the original task, but the output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/0/code.py:46:#    The marker color varies across samples and is not red. In many samples red is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D9/1/code.py:243:    Paint each walled-off region with a cyclic frame pattern, then let the center color spill across walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D9/1/code.py:251:    - Second, inspect the finished first-pass picture: each region's deepest layer color crosses any shared wall and overwrites the neighboring region's wall-adjacent outer layer by one cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D9/1/code.py:279:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/2/code.py:56:#    Across 2-4 examples a human should see two linked effects: bars are reordered by height\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D10/0/code.py:45:#   sprite lookup code must switch from color-keyed matching to shape-keyed recolor + target-keyed placement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/1/code.py:139:    - Red (2) singleton embedded in a component means: reflect payload across that pixel's row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/1/code.py:140:    - Blue (1) singleton embedded in a component means: reflect payload across that pixel's column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D7/2/code.py:59:#     - Across examples, the solver still clearly \"moves plug onto base\", but the output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/4/code.py:16:#   several same-width monochrome vertical bars that cross the baseline and have\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/4/code.py:62:#   Across examples, the input visibly shows different bar heights and shuffled\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D5/4/code.py:69:#     identical across rows. The generator guarantees that by drawing solid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:11:#     new_hub: 6x6 thick cross made from five 2x2 blocks:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:20:#       - C is a fifth neutral hub-center color used only to keep the cross 4-connected\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:27:#       - mirror symmetry across the contact axis\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:36:#   structural/positional: square perimeter -> radial cross arms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:40:# - The neutral 2x2 center is necessary; without it the four arm colors cannot form one connected cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:48:# These are replaced by an explicit 6x6 cross detector and four arm-tip contact specs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:54:# - The cross occupies 20 cells inside a 6x6 bbox and has four empty 2x2 corners, so it is visually\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:58:# - Exactly one near-center 6x6 thick cross exists.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:152:def _find_cross_hub(g: np.ndarray, bg: int):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:157:            # The four 2x2 corners must be background so the 6x6 bbox visibly reads as a cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D5/1/code.py:232:    hub = _find_cross_hub(g, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/0/code.py:230:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/3/code.py:146:    - Mirror the whole sprite across that axis. Originals and red controls remain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:13:#       Each target is an interior crosshair:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:15:#       - one short perpendicular tick crossing the rail,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:16:#       - a colored center pixel at the crossing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:33:#       A horizontal rail on row 6 with crosshair center at (6, 9) means the marker must end\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:36:#       so the generator switches to one sprite per crosshair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:46:#       shared orientation. The dataset still varies orientation across samples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:50:#       - \"anchor is an isolated singleton\": false now, because the center is embedded in a crosshair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:72:#       - crosshair centers as the destinations,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:78:#     That avoids clutter near the rails and keeps the new crosshair cue unambiguous.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:92:    Slide multi-color sprites along interior crosshair rails until their marker pixels reach the matching centers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:96:    - One or more interior crosshairs: a long monochrome rail plus a short perpendicular tick, with a colored center pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:97:    - Multi-color sprites whose minority-color marker matches one crosshair center color; only the marker sits on that rail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:100:    - Detect each crosshair by its long rail, then match sprites to the center pixel sharing the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/1/code.py:104:    Key insight: The long internal line, not the border, now encodes the motion axis and target location; the colored crossing pixel is the destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/291dc1e1/D1/0/code.py:58:#    cross the masked edge row/column. The transformed variants are produced by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:43:- `placeholder_colors` used to come from one crop. Now colors must be aggregated across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:90:    total blocks across all frames: 6-10\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/0/code.py:165:    Key insight: The external clues are still global, but the placeholders are partitioned across several independent frames, so the solver must first assign each color to the correct frame before stamping the sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/0/code.py:36:#         across the strip thickness: left border in a vertical strip, top border in a horizontal strip;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D4/0/code.py:54:#     - the target palette is small (3 colors per sample) and reused across many holes, which avoids a noisy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/1/code.py:185:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/2/code.py:91:    Every non-red, non-background 4-connected component is mirrored across it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/0/code.py:60:#    slots share the same color. This makes the change visible across only a few\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/0/code.py:117:    Sort vertical bars by height and redistribute them across fixed x-slots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D8/0/code.py:354:        # Now verify exactly 1 valid attachment across all 4 rotations x 4 sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2c181942/D8/0/code.py:358:        # We need exactly 1 such (rotation, side) pair across all possibilities.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D14/2/code.py:41:#      local regularities across examples rather than too many degrees of freedom.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D14/2/code.py:66:#    - Across examples, horizontal lines yield tall stacked outputs; vertical lines\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D14/2/code.py:79:#         * one full straight separator line across the canvas\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:15:#      outline around an irregular enclosed region shaped like an L or a cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:23:#      corner of that 4 x 4 box lies outside the L/cross interior, those sprite pixels\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:26:#    - Shape family is limited to two visible categories: L and cross. This keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:39:#      interior mask or they would leak across the missing corners / arms.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:42:#      intersection with the interior is 4-connected, non-empty, and still spans the full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:47:#    - At least one placeholder is visibly truncated by the L/cross boundary, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:366:    \"\"\"Return valid slot boxes whose intersection with the irregular interior stays bbox-sized.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:395:    \"\"\"Build an L or cross interior mask whose valid slot count stays in range.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:398:        shape_type = random.choice([\"L\", \"cross\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D11/1/code.py:400:        if shape_type == \"cross\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/3/code.py:48:#     - Anchor colors stay limited to 1-3 and are reused across 3-5 sprites, so each sample\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/3/code.py:72:#     - The generator mixes top/bottom and left/right anchors and reuses colors across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D8/1/code.py:26:#       This keeps the visual effect obvious across 2-4 examples without introducing arbitrary\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/4a21e3da/D13/1/code.py:57:    non-local comparison across multiple candidate regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/13e47133/D2/2/code.py:211:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:28:#      repeated marker color per grid and splits that color across both anchors of its pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:49:#    - Because at least one color is reused and split across both anchors, the \"choose nearer\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:50:#      branch is usually demonstrated within a single grid instead of relying only on cross-grid\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:29:#      Input may contain 4 bars crossing the baseline plus 2 floating 2x2 blocks in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py:32:#      components crossing the baseline and matching the solid centered-rectangle bar\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/31f7f899/D9/3/code.py