r draws a cross of full-span dividers, keeps legends inside their own subpanels with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D9/2/code.py:34:#    This guarantees no sprite crosses a partition line and every sprite has an unambiguous local legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D9/2/code.py:36:#    Region dependence is carried by visible geometry only: the cross partition and the legend subpanels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D9/2/code.py:38:#    hole count across regions plus cross-region distractors so the local rule is inferable from 2-3 grids.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D9/2/code.py:43:#    Only four legend colors are used per grid, two per region. The same hole count is duplicated across\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D9/2/code.py:49:#   partition: exactly one full row and one full column of divider color, forming a cross\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D9/2/code.py:149:    assert len(legend_sides) == 1, \"legend groups must occupy exactly one side of the cross\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D9/2/code.py:200:        assert pr != div_r and pc != div_c, \"sprite must not lie on the divider cross\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D9/2/code.py:316:def _cross_layout(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D9/2/code.py:540:    # Generation only needs one guaranteed match per local legend entry plus one cross-region distractor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D9/2/code.py:572:    uniques = {region: next(iter(local_holes[region] - set.intersection(*local_holes.values()))) for region in region_keys}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e3721c99/D9/2/code.py:603:    rects, region_to_legend_rect, legends_by_rect, _arrangement = _cross_layout(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/332f06d7/D6/1/code.py:32:#      reachable/stuck samples across calls instead of leaving the split fully random.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7b3084d4/D7/1/code.py:273:    if 